Well, since I got lucky on a blind guess once, let's
even out the score by being dead wrong on another
one.

It sounds like what you have is a font-choice issue,
or perhaps more correctly a "code sheet"-choice
issue, with the games being played with a font that
uses some nice glyphs for wall drawing; the old
IBM-PC font was one such, it had all the symbols
needed to mix and match single and double ruled
boxes made out of text glyphs, which make for very
dressy dungeon walls. If even the floor
characters are messed up, your originals are
probably using raised centered dots, which look a
lot dressier than the standard periods, but happen
not to be ASCII characters.

What you'll need to do, I'm guessing, is identify
with someone using the same recorded games you are,
what font and code sheet is being used in the window
that displays them, and then get a matching font or
code sheet attached to your rxvt window.

This should have been enough of a hint for someone
closer to the problem to put you on the correct
path.

